course: dictionary
lesson: 11878
title: Bragging and showing off
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Bragging means talking proudly about yourself and what you have or can do, in a way that annoys other people. Another word for it is boasting. Look at the words around it: «Mia kept bragging about her goal, and nobody wanted to hear it» tells you she talked on and on about herself, and the others were fed up.
explain: Bragging can be a noun, as in «Nobody likes bragging.» It can also be the -ing form of the verb brag, as in «The boys were bragging all day.» The other forms are brag, brags and bragged, as in «Sam bragged about his new bike.»
explain: Bragging is not the same as being proud. Being proud of your work is fine. Bragging is when you talk about it so that others feel small. Context clues such as «annoys» or «rolled their eyes» help you tell the difference.
explain: «Ben won the quiz, so he got bragging rights for the whole week.» Bragging rights is a phrase used after a game or contest. It means the right to boast because you won.
fact: Bragging means talking proudly about yourself in a way that annoys other people.
fact: Bragging is another word for boasting.
fact: Bragging can be a noun or the -ing form of the verb brag.
fact: The other forms are brag, brags and bragged: «He bragged about his score.»
fact: Bragging rights are the right to boast because you won.
exercise: «Mia kept bragging about her goal, and nobody wanted to hear it.» What does bragging mean here? | Kicking the ball very hard | *Talking proudly about herself in a way that annoys others | Telling a sad story about a lost game | Practising quietly on her own
exercise: «Ben won the quiz, so he got bragging rights for the week.» What are bragging rights? | A prize of money | *The right to boast because you won | A rule about who sits at the front | A sore throat from shouting
exercise: Which word means the same as bragging? | Practising | Whispering | *Boasting | Sleeping
test: Ravi says, «Look at me, I'm the best at everything!» What is Ravi doing? | Asking for help | Singing | *Bragging | Joking gently
test: In «The boys were bragging all day», what is bragging? | A type of bird | A colour | *The -ing form of the verb brag | A place name
exam: Which sentence shows bragging? | «Dan said sorry and shared his lunch.» | *«Dan kept telling us he was the fastest and never let anyone else speak.» | «Dan cheered for his friends.» | «Dan helped me pick up the books.»
